# rule.always.fix-forward-under-scouts-honor

> **when you see a small, safe, clean fix — do it now. never defer it.**

too big → catch a dream (+ a fulcrum if the deferral was a JUDGMENT). pair: `rule.always.catch-dreams-for-followups`.

two questions, which grade the FIX, never the scope:
1. SAFE? no behavior beyond what you came for, no risk to work you cannot see
2. CLEAN? lands in the diff you have, with no ripple to other files, contracts, callers

safe + clean → pull it in now. safe, not clean → dream + fulcrum. unsafe → dream + fulcrum. "i wasn't asked" and "later stone" are not among the questions.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| typo, stale comment, dead line, wrong path in a file you touched | fix it |
| about to write "we should also…" / "i'll flag that" | do it this turn, or catch a dream |
| real work (rename across files, contract change, migration) | dream + fulcrum |
| unsure it is small | try it; a revert is cheap |
| round ends with more dreams than repairs | default was inverted; audit |
blocker: a small safe clean fix seen and deferred · a deferral with no caught dream · a dirt deferral with no fulcrum · a rippled change smuggled in (fails CLEAN) · the batch (small fixes saved for the end).
